  "_materials_comment": "points: typical relative core loss [f Hz, B̂ T, Pv kW/m³] at 100 °C from the material data sheet. beta: flux exponent — measured where the sheet gives two flux levels at one frequency (3F36), otherwise the usual MnZn power-ferrite value (beta_source says which). The loss model normalises every point to 0.1 T with beta and interpolates log-log in frequency, so the local alpha at fsw comes from the neighbouring points. alpha_from: borrow the frequency slope of another material when the sheet gives only one frequency.",
